[center][size=6][color=#d597ff]BabelChat[/color][/size]
[size=4]Break the language barrier in World of Warcraft[/size][/center]

[center][url=https://yumatech.ru/donate/][img]https://img.shields.io/badge/Donate-USDT%20%7C%20OpenCollective-blue[/img][/url][/center]

[size=5][color=#FFD200]☕ The Problem[/color][/size]

You join a PUG raid. The tank explains tactics — in Spanish. The healer asks something — in German. Nobody understands each other. Sound familiar?

[b]BabelChat fixes this.[/b] It translates WoW chat in real time — gaming terms instantly (built in), and full sentences via an optional free companion app.

[size=5][color=#FFD200]🚀 Quick Start[/color][/size]

[list=1]
[*][b]Install the addon.[/b] That's it — gaming terms (lfm, brez, gilded, M+, delves…) now translate automatically right in your chat. [b]No setup, no keys, no account, completely free.[/b]
[*][b]Pick your language[/b] (optional): type [b]/babel config[/b] and choose your language.
[*][b]Want full-sentence translation too?[/b] (optional) Download the [b]free[/b] companion app from GitHub — see the Companion App section below. The dictionary keeps working with or without it.
[/list]

[i]New here? Just install and play — step 1 already does the most useful part for free.[/i]

[size=5][color=#FFD200]🔑 Key Features[/color][/size]

[b]Standalone — addon only (100% free, no account):[/b]
[list]
[*][b]380+ gaming terms[/b] translated in 14 languages — lfm, wts, dps, ez, copium, delves, gilded, M+, RIO…
[*]Clean annotation below the original message (no inline color spam)
[*]13 categories incl. a current [b]Endgame & Midnight[/b] set (delves, crests, gear tracks, Warbands)
[*]Hyperlink-aware — never breaks item/spell/achievement links
[*]Works out of the box, [b]no API keys needed[/b]
[/list]

[b]With the optional companion app (also free):[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Full sentence translation[/b] of live chat
[*]Smart overlay on top of WoW with channel colors
[*]Streaming — original shows instantly, translation arrives 0.5-2s later
[*]Read-only memory access — never writes, injects, or automates
[*]Choose your provider: [b]DeepL[/b] or [b]Microsoft Translator[/b] (see below)
[/list]

[size=5][color=#FFD200]💳 "Is the app free? Why a credit card?"[/color][/size]

[b]Yes — BabelChat (addon and companion) is free and always will be.[/b] The companion just needs a translation provider's API key:

[list]
[*][b]DeepL[/b] — free tier (500,000 chars/month). DeepL asks for a credit card to [i]verify[/i] the account; [b]it never charges you[/b] on the free tier. That prompt comes from DeepL, not BabelChat.
[*][b]Microsoft Translator[/b] — free tier (2M chars/month), [b]no credit card required[/b]. Pick this if you'd rather not give DeepL a card.
[/list]

